        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="0316" n="232" xml:id="pg232"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr. Ehrman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-11-04"><hi rendition="#italic">November 4, 1903</hi></date>.
                        (Sent 12.02 p.m.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Communicate with commander of gunboat <hi rendition="#italic">Bogotá</hi> and
                    state plainly that this Government, being responsible for maintaining peace and
                    keeping transit open across Isthmus, desires him to refrain from wantonly
                    shelling the city. We shall have a naval force at Panama in two days, and are
                    now ordering men from the <hi rendition="#italic">Nashville</hi> to Panama in
                    the interests of peace.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Loomis.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
